TOPIC 7 : DIFFERENCE BETWEEN CONTINUOUS INTEGRATION (CI),
           CONTINUOUS DELIVERY (CD), AND CONTINUOUS DEPLOYMENT
======================================================================

Q1. Differentiate between Continuous Integration (CI), Continuous
Delivery (CD), and Continuous Deployment.

Interview Ready Answer

Continuous Integration (CI) focuses on integrating code changes
frequently into a shared repository where every commit is automatically
built and tested.

Continuous Delivery (CD) extends CI by automatically preparing the
application for release. The application is always in a deployable state,
but deployment to production requires manual approval.

Continuous Deployment extends Continuous Delivery by automatically
deploying every successful build to the production environment without
any manual approval.

======================================================================

